  "name": "Instruction-Following & Format Adherence",
  "description": "Verifiable instruction-following in the style of IFEval: each prompt stacks multiple machine-checkable constraints (length bounds, exact counts, forbidden characters/words, strict JSON, custom markup, positional rules). Graded on constraint compliance rather than content, so no judge is needed. Every item is gated on a loose check proving the task was attempted, so a prohibition can never be satisfied by an empty answer. The gate is never the constraint under measurement -- a near-miss keeps partial credit, only a non-attempt scores zero. Original items; difficulty comes from stacking individually-clear constraints, never from ambiguous wording.",
